# Line endings, made explicit.
#
# This repository has always stored text as LF — all 612 tracked text blobs were verified LF-only
# when this file was added — but it achieved that through every clone happening to have
# core.autocrlf=true. Nothing in the repository said so, so a clone with autocrlf=false would
# commit CRLF and no one would notice until a diff came back entirely rewritten.
#
# text=auto makes that guarantee the repository's own, independent of each developer's git config:
# git normalises to LF on commit and converts to the platform convention on checkout. Because
# storage is already LF, adding this renormalises nothing.
#
# This matters beyond tidiness here. Three files carried MIXED endings in the working tree, and
# mixed endings have already produced a silent no-op edit in this project: a revert regex written
# against \n did not match a CRLF file, and a test briefly looked verified when it was not. The
# sibling mobile repos are CRLF working trees, which is why resume-master-android hashes
# CHECKSUMS.json over LF-normalised content rather than raw bytes.
* text=auto

# Binary assets: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
